{
  "comment": "N-041 shared WhatsOnChain getContractUtxo + getTransaction vectors (companion of vectors.json, F-040). getContractUtxo(scriptHash) reads GET {base}/script/{scriptHash}/unspent, which WoC serves as a legacy JSON array [{height,tx_pos,tx_hash,value}] or, on the /unspent/all family, as an object {script, result:[...]}; both shapes are accepted. Neither carries the locking script, so the SDK fetches GET {base}/tx/{txid}/hex for the first entry, requires double-SHA256(body) reversed == txid, tx_pos to be an output, the 8-byte output value to equal the listed value, a non-empty script, and sha256(script) reversed == scriptHash (WoC's scripthash convention). An empty listing or a 404 listing means no UTXO (null). getTransaction(txid) reads GET {base}/tx/{txid}/hex (never /tx/hash/{txid}, whose JSON has no hex field and float BTC values), hash-verifies it and parses inputs/outputs exactly; raw is the served hex.",
  "provenance": "Recorded 2026-09-29T21:07Z-21:09Z from https://api.whatsonchain.com/v1/bsv/main by F-040 (raw bodies in remediation-logs/F-040/vectors/). contractUtxo.legacyBody and objectBody are the first two entries of the recorded /script/{h}/unspent and /script/{h}/unspent/all bodies, re-serialized compactly in the served key order; rawTxHex and hashBody are verbatim. The large-value tx, its hashBody and every rejection vector are synthetic.",
